{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"28f23b1c29684f7fc0c9a8fbac0f084a278c7745ea5c81d8b9d662fe9a127da6","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / plan-relation snapshot","key_entities":["plan-relation-snapshot-error","reducer-error","rebar review-plan",".tickets-tracker","CREATE event","SNAPSHOT event","_store/event_append._prepare_event","PlanRelationSnapshotError","os.makedirs"],"problem_keywords":["plan-relation reducer","event-less ticket","empty directory","plan review","indeterminate verdict","store artifact","reducer error"],"propositions":["A ticket directory with no CREATE or SNAPSHOT event causes the plan-relation reducer to fail, surfacing as INDETERMINATE verdict on unrelated tickets in the same epic.","Empty ticket directories are created when a write process dies between makedirs and atomic event rename, persist locally invisible to git, and block plan reviews of unrelated tickets.","The plan-relation reducer should skip event-less directories with a warning rather than failing the snapshot, allowing reviews to proceed on unrelated tickets.","The writer-side fix of removing the directory before its first event is not viable because it cannot cover process-death orphans and would race concurrent writers."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787564288563461001,"uuid":"132dcd69-1330-4bf7-ba1c-aad21325cbae"}